From: =?UTF-8?q?S=C3=A9bastien=20Celles?= <s.celles@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 08:55:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 32/62] verimark: IT-specific ClientHello builder (5 ciphers,
 no 0x00a9)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The IT firmware rejects ClientHellos containing cipher 0x00a9 with
a fatal illegal_parameter Alert. The DT builder
verimark_tls_build_client_hello advertises 6 ciphers including
0x00a9 — fine for the DT, not for the IT.

verimark_tls_build_client_hello_it builds the 78-byte IT variant :
same shape as the DT version, with 5 ciphers (c0 05 c0 2e 00 3d
00 8d 00 a8) instead of 6. Layout differences :

  record length  0x0049  vs DT 0x004b
  HS length      0x0045  vs DT 0x0047
  cs_len         0x000a  vs DT 0x000c

Verbatim against the documented device trace structure (frame 4172 — the
ClientHello sent by the Windows driver during the captured fresh
pairing) — runtime-validated end-to-end 2026-06-07 via
tools/verimark-it/handshake_attempt.py --probe-appdata.

Tests added in test_tls.c (3 new, 18 total green) :
- build_client_hello_it_byte_by_byte
- build_client_hello_it_buffer_too_small
- build_client_hello_it_diff_with_dt (asserts the 5 cipher bytes
  and that the byte immediately after is comp_meth_len = 0x00, not
  the dropped 0xa9)

Test vector TV_HS_CLIENT_HELLO_IT_RECORD added to test_vectors.h
(78 bytes, derived from the DT vector with the 5-cipher layout and
the same fixed test client_random for reproducibility).
